  "summary": "Accelerator (throttle) cable from the firewall to the carburetor, all models. At the firewall the cable flange is held by a screw assembly and washer; a plate is riveted at the cable hole. At the carburetor the cable passes through a bracket held under a carburetor attaching nut, is clamped to that bracket with a bolt, and its end snaps on a ball stud nutted to the throttle lever, with a return spring and grease.",
